@node Overview
@chapter Overview

Basalt Deep Learning is a portable C++20 deep-learning framework licensed
under the GNU General Public License version 3 or later (GPLv3+).  It is
built on top of the @emph{Bellows} C++ machine-learning library and its
transitive @emph{Hyper Math} scientific computing engine.

Basalt Deep Learning adheres strictly to the GNU Coding Standards as an
engineering, formatting, build-system, and documentation discipline.  It is
an independent project and is @strong{not} part of, endorsed by, or
affiliated with the GNU Project.

@section Key Capabilities
@itemize @bullet
@item
Multi-dtype N-dimensional strided @code{basalt::Tensor} with zero-copy views
and NumPy/PyTorch-compatible broadcasting over Bellows @code{slab_buffer}
arenas.
@item
Dynamic reverse-mode automatic differentiation with higher-order derivatives
(@code{create_graph = true}), @code{No_Grad_Guard}, @code{Enable_Grad_Guard},
activation @code{checkpoint}, and finite-difference @code{gradcheck}.
@item
Comprehensive @code{basalt::nn} module library including @code{Linear},
@code{Conv1d}/@code{2d}/@code{3d}, pooling, @code{Batch_Norm},
@code{Layer_Norm}, @code{Group_Norm}, @code{RMS_Norm},
@code{Multihead_Attention}, @code{Transformer_Encoder}, and
@code{Transformer_Decoder}.
@item
First-order and adaptive optimizers (@code{SGD}, @code{Adam}, @code{AdamW},
@code{RMSprop}, @code{Adagrad}, @code{LAMB}) and learning-rate schedulers
(@code{Step_LR}, @code{Cosine_Annealing_LR}, @code{One_Cycle_LR},
@code{Linear_Warmup_LR}, @code{Reduce_LR_On_Plateau}).
@item
Versioned FNV-1a checksummed checkpoints (@file{.bckpt}), Hugging Face
Safetensors (@file{.safetensors}), and ONNX (@file{.onnx}) import/export.
@item
Lightning-style @code{basalt::Trainer}, mixed precision (@code{Float16} and
@code{BFloat16}), multi-device @code{Data_Parallel}, a stable C ABI
(@code{libbasalt-c}), CLI utilities (@command{basalt-train},
@command{basalt-inspect}, @command{basalt-convert}), and optional
@code{pybind11} Python bindings (@code{import basalt}).
@end itemize

@node Tutorial
@chapter Tutorial

@section Building and Installing
Basalt Deep Learning uses the standard GNU Autotools workflow:

@example
./configure --prefix=/usr/local
make -j4
make check
make install
@end example

@section Training a Model in C++20
Include @code{<basalt/basalt.hpp>}, subclass @code{basalt::Trainable_Module},
and pass a @code{basalt::data::Data_Loader} to @code{basalt::Trainer::fit}:

@example
#include <basalt/basalt.hpp>

int
main (void)
@{
  basalt::seed_everything (42);
  basalt::Tensor x = basalt::randn (@{32, 4@});
  basalt::Tensor w = basalt::randn (@{4, 1@}).set_requires_grad (true);
  basalt::Tensor y = basalt::ops::matmul (x, w);
  basalt::Tensor loss = basalt::ops::mean (basalt::ops::square (y));
  loss.backward ();
  return 0;
@}
@end example

@node Internals
@chapter Internals

@section Bellows Engine Integration
Basalt Deep Learning never duplicates functionality already provided by
Bellows or Hyper Math:
@itemize @bullet
@item
CPU memory allocations are backed by 64-byte aligned
@code{hyper_math::slab_buffer<uint8_t>} inside
@code{basalt::bellows_compat::Bellows_Storage}.
@item
Parallel tensor kernels, batched GEMM, convolutions, and data-loader workers
execute on @code{hyper_math::parallel_for} and @code{hyper_math::thread_pool}.
@item
Random number generation wraps @code{hyper_math::random_engine} (PCG64).
@item
Orthogonal weight initialization delegates to
@code{hyper_math::scientific::linalg::qr}.
@item
Tabular dataset normalization delegates to
@code{bellows::moment_normaliser}, evaluation metrics delegate to
@code{bellows::evaluation}, and checkpoint integrity uses
@code{bellows::compute_fnv1a_checksum}.
@end itemize

@section Dynamic Reverse-Mode Autograd
Every differentiable operation constructs an @code{Autograd_Node} on the
dynamic computation graph when @code{Grad_Mode::is_enabled ()} is true and any
operand has @code{requires_grad () == true}.  Calling @code{backward ()}
performs a topological sort from the root outputs, accumulates gradients into
leaf @code{Autograd_Meta} slots, and verifies @code{Saved_Variable} version
counters to catch illegal in-place mutations.

